{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1041 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0359c4aa59c87c6bdc2f256a480da609852785b565836ef52eadea3015608ed7" :edb/db-before-t 1040 :edb/db-after-t 1041 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534353 50 #inst "2026-10-06T16:40:37.382Z" 13194139534353 true] [17592186119876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283927 13194139534353 true] [17592186119876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283934 13194139534353 true] [17592186119878 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283941 13194139534353 true] [17592186119878 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283948 13194139534353 true] [17592186120337 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534353 true] [17592186120337 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x) = \\frac{4x^{2} - 3x}{8x - 6}$." 13194139534353 false] [17592186120337 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x}{8x-6}.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186120337 1145 "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x}{8x-6} & =\\frac{x(4x-3)}{2(4x-3)}=\\frac{x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987351/assets/3e6ebc8eaec86276442b13fde934234fdaf9c4a457398bb1b792c6910350e44c.png)" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283927 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283928 13194139534353 true] [17592186283927 1089 "q-107028" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283927 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534353 true] [17592186283927 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{4x-12}{3{x}^{2}-9x}.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283927 1113 #uuid "2d9af6b9-98f5-5715-92c9-adf8a60f68c2" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283927 1145 "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-12}{3{x}^{2}-9x} & =\\frac{4(x-3)}{3x(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cancel{(x-3)}}{3x\\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n3x=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=0.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283929 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283930 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283931 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283932 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283933 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1041 "selection" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283932 13194139534353 true] [17592186283928 1110 #uuid "9b32fa74-de1e-5cb0-b480-8bb23cc82da9" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283929 1034 "$x=0$, $x=4$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283929 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534353 true] [17592186283929 1111 #uuid "a5243f75-fbc3-56f0-afc7-5139aaa8a5e9" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283930 1034 "x=3" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283930 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283930 1111 #uuid "8a5b9a41-65b9-5367-ad9c-6d66393dff80" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283931 1034 "x=4" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283931 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283931 1111 #uuid "e2984acc-d8c8-5543-a72c-acb45746e5d5" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283932 1034 "x=0" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283932 1111 #uuid "2457603d-e191-53b7-adfd-3405462093b2" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283933 1034 "$x=0$, $x=3$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534353 true] [17592186283933 1111 #uuid "f9de4aa8-9bc4-52a6-9755-3d0f17e6e3e7" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283934 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283935 13194139534353 true] [17592186283934 1089 "q-4630" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283934 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534353 true] [17592186283934 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-x-1}.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283934 1113 #uuid "7eabb1cc-388e-58ab-a506-5be08d869744" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283934 1145 "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x-3}{2{x}^{2}-x-1} & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+3)}{(2x+1)(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)}(x+3)}{(2x+1)\\cancel{(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+3}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n2x+1=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283936 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283937 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283938 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283939 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283940 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1041 "selection" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283940 13194139534353 true] [17592186283935 1110 #uuid "d91d0606-c2ac-5733-8d67-c9b1eaea9069" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283936 1034 "No vertical asymptotes" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534353 true] [17592186283936 1111 #uuid "923b89ec-5094-5b83-8a84-1b6c36541985" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283937 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,x=1" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283937 1111 #uuid "ff960184-cde7-5164-8b96-04baa11d6b06" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283938 1034 "x=-3,\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283938 1111 #uuid "0b94819d-3eb7-5e8b-bcc2-6f3e7b326da1" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283939 1034 "x=-1,\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283939 1111 #uuid "5495de14-a447-55dd-87d6-cc6708ee40c9" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283940 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283940 1111 #uuid "d860eb09-c882-5a35-8bb8-6f104ab1f17e" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283941 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283942 13194139534353 true] [17592186283941 1089 "q-73029" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283941 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534353 true] [17592186283941 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{1}{x-6}.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283941 1113 #uuid "866875d0-d558-5de5-a3c8-64626804b8ba" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283941 1145 "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{1}{x-6} & =\\frac{x-6-(x+3)}{(x+3)(x-6)}=-\\frac{9}{(x+3)(x-6)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n(x+3)(x-6)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3\\,,\\,x=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=-3$ and $x=6.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283943 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283944 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283945 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283946 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283947 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1041 "selection" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283947 13194139534353 true] [17592186283942 1110 #uuid "0b60a928-3f7b-5f55-b8e6-817717e01424" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283943 1034 "x=3" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283943 1111 #uuid "b58a571e-febe-5c28-ad42-3733cddb28db" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283944 1034 "x=-3" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283944 1111 #uuid "1e31c918-96a0-58cb-a562-c6630cdae6a2" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283945 1034 "x=6" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534353 true] [17592186283945 1111 #uuid "6a13f398-0e30-5764-92e6-1709e66d7ad2" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283946 1034 "$x=-6$, $x=3$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534353 true] [17592186283946 1111 #uuid "cd9b5bc9-a132-543f-bc09-4f0b97076cb2" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283947 1034 "$x=-3$, $x=6$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534353 true] [17592186283947 1111 #uuid "e788baba-bfb5-5a25-a9de-0326600cc34e" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283948 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283949 13194139534353 true] [17592186283948 1089 "q-73031" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283948 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534353 true] [17592186283948 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+1}.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283948 1113 #uuid "70dea798-f51a-5943-b982-89e197a7bc77" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283948 1145 "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+1} & =\\frac{x+1+(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}=\\frac{2x}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n(x-1)(x+1)=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\\,,\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=1$ and $x=-1.$" 13194139534353 true] [17592186283949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283950 13194139534353 true] [17592186283949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283951 13194139534353 true] [17592186283949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283952 13194139534353 true] [17592186283949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283953 13194139534353 true] [1759